# .semgrepignore — scoped noise suppression for the reconciliation-workflow-agent scan.
#
# This file suppresses findings by PATH ONLY (gitignore syntax); semgrep reads it
# automatically. It CANNOT filter by rule ID — for that, pass the noise rule IDs below to
# `semgrep --exclude-rule <id>` (or the scanner's equivalent). Both halves were triaged from
# ProbeScanExport-b6ca1602 (2026-07-26): 3 genuine issues fixed (commit 92e9ae1); everything
# listed here is style/i18n/vendored noise, NOT a security finding.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOISE RULE IDs (suppress via --exclude-rule; NOT effective in this file):
#   jsx-not-internationalized          # 279 — app has no i18n requirement (internal tooling UI)
#   react-props-spreading              #  99 — team style choice, not a vulnerability
#   missing-template-string-indicator  #  28 — false positives in test literals (swarmParser.test)
#   no-stringify-keys                  #  22 — style/perf micro-lint
#   react-props-in-state               #   1 — style
#   useless-assignment                 #   2 — dead-code lint (not security)
#   useless-ternary                    #   1 — style
#   prefer-json-notation               #   1 — style
#   code-after-unconditional-return    #   1 — dead-code lint
#
# Example invocation:
#   semgrep --config auto \
#     --exclude-rule jsx-not-internationalized \
#     --exclude-rule react-props-spreading \
#     --exclude-rule missing-template-string-indicator \
#     --exclude-rule no-stringify-keys \
#     --exclude-rule react-props-in-state \
#     --exclude-rule useless-assignment \
#     --exclude-rule useless-ternary \
#     --exclude-rule prefer-json-notation \
#     --exclude-rule code-after-unconditional-return
#
# Deliberately NOT suppressed (real security signal — keep scanning): detect-non-literal-fs-filename,
# path-join-resolve-traversal, no-iam-data-exfiltration, unsafe-formatstring, secret-in-build-arg,
# aws-access-token, detected-jwt-token, generic-api-key, insecure-innerhtml, *postmessage*,
# unsafe-dynamic-method, detect-insecure-websocket, aws-lambda-permission-unrestricted-source-arn,
# and all aws-*-unencrypted / hardening rules.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

